ESP_Octopus
- Board role: Wi-Fi access point, web portal, Octopus serial bridge, light PWM controller
- Wi-Fi AP SSID: ESP_Octopus
- Wi-Fi AP password: octopus123
- Fixed IP: 192.168.4.1
- UART to Octopus board:
  - GPIO16 -> RX from Octopus TX
  - GPIO17 -> TX to Octopus RX
- Light PWM output:
  - GPIO18 -> PWM output for all 6 lamps through transistor/MOSFET driver

ESP_Remote
- Board role: handheld remote with 7 push buttons, fixed-IP Wi-Fi client
- Fixed IP: 192.168.4.2
- Gateway / ESP_Octopus IP: 192.168.4.1
- Buttons use INPUT_PULLUP and are active-low:
  - GPIO13 -> Lights On
  - GPIO14 -> Lights Off
  - GPIO25 -> Pos1
  - GPIO26 -> Pos2
  - GPIO27 -> Random Position
  - GPIO32 -> Dimmer / hold-to-change-brightness
  - GPIO33 -> Spare / reserved

Notes
- Do not drive the lamps directly from GPIO18. Use a proper transistor or MOSFET stage sized for the lamp current.
- The dimmer button changes brightness in steps while held. On release, direction flips for the next hold.
- Browser control is hosted by ESP_Octopus at http://192.168.4.1/
